From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(ssd/l2): add L2 expert cache scaffolding (inert
 without P2P)

NOTE: This is a structural reference patch, not a git-am-ready file.
The hunk headers and line numbers are approximate. The functions
listed here are meant to be inserted into ds4_cuda.cu right after the
existing cuda_stream_expert_cache_release_all (around line 23280 in
the committed state at 85512d5) and before the parallel pool code
that starts around line 23825. Re-validate the insertion points with
`grep -n` before applying.



Adds the data structures and primitive helpers for an L2 expert cache
on a peer tier (GPU1 in TP+SSD mode). All entry points are gated on
g_gpu_peer_ok[primary_tier][l2_tier] && g_gpu_peer_ok[l2_tier][primary_tier]
so the entire feature is silently inactive on GeForce / no-P2P
hardware.

Adds:
  - struct cuda_stream_load_pool gains l2_cache, l2_tier, l2_mutex,
    l2_hits / l2_misses / l2_writes counters.
  - cuda_stream_l2_tier_for(primary): returns the lowest tier != primary
    if P2P is two-way enabled; -1 otherwise.
  - cuda_stream_l2_ensure(primary, gate_bytes, down_bytes): lazily
    allocate the L2 cache on the L2 tier via the existing
    cuda_stream_expert_cache_prepare.
  - cuda_stream_l2_fetch_into_primary(): lookup + peer-copy L2 -> claimed
    primary slot, publish primary slot metadata.
  - cuda_stream_l2_write_through(): peer-copy primary slot -> L2 slot,
    with claim-flag serialisation.
  - cuda_xdev_copy_raw(): raw-pointer peer copy wrapper that uses
    cudaMemcpyPeer when P2P is available, transparent BOUNCE otherwise.
  - cuda_stream_expert_cache_release_all_at(): release helper that
    takes an explicit cache pointer (the existing release_all operates
    on ssd_current()).

The L2 helpers are not yet called from anywhere — that's patch 0003.

